title: Microsoft Intune: Apple VPP Tokens
agents: special
catalog: cloud/microsoft
license: GPLv2
distribution: Christopher Pommer
description:
 This check monitors the status and expiration of Apple VPP (Volume Purchase Program)
 tokens configured in Microsoft Intune.

 The check processes data collected by the {Microsoft Intune} special agent, which
 queries the Microsoft Graph API to retrieve information about all configured VPP
 tokens in the Intune tenant.

 VPP tokens have both a validity state and an expiration date. The service monitors
 both aspects:

 Token validity state:

 - {Token state "valid"}: Normal expiration monitoring applies

 - {Any other token state}: Service immediately reports CRIT regardless of expiration

 Expiration monitoring (when token state is "valid"):

 {OK}: Token expires in more than 14 days

 {WARN}: Token expires within 14 days

 {CRIT}: Token expires within 5 days

 For expired tokens, the service continues to report critical state and displays
 the expiration timespan as "X ago" format.

 The service details include complete token information such as expiration time,
 token name, unique token ID, token state, and associated Apple ID for administrative
 reference.

 You must configure the {Microsoft Intune} special agent to collect Apple VPP
 token data from your Intune tenant.

item:
 The name of the Apple VPP token as configured in Intune. If multiple tokens
 share the same name, the last 4 characters of the token ID are appended
 for unique identification (e.g., "Token 1 a1b2").

discovery:
 One service is created automatically for each Apple VPP token found in the
 Intune tenant. Services are named "Intune Apple VPP token {token_name}" where
 {token_name} is the configured token name, potentially with ID suffix for uniqueness.